<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Croatian–Ottoman wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">15th–16th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Croatian–Ottoman wars were a long series of conflicts between the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> from the fifteenth century to the end of the sixteenth. Ottoman raids and conquests, including the victory at Krbava Field in 1493, reduced Croatia to a narrow remnant. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> organised the Military Frontier, and the Croatian victory at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sisak">Sisak</a> in 1593 halted the Ottoman advance.</p></div>
